# =============================================================================
# Line endings
# =============================================================================
# Normalise to LF in the repository, and check out LF everywhere. This matters
# because a shell script with CRLF line endings fails at runtime with an obscure
# `\r: command not found`, and this repo is meant to be forked — including by
# people on Windows. All current files are already LF, so this is a no-op today
# and a guard tomorrow.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# =============================================================================
# Language statistics (GitHub Linguist)
# =============================================================================
# This is a Node/Express backend. The language bar should say so.
#
# Coverage reports are jest output, not source. They were committed once in
# f2cedf5 (218 KB of lcov-report HTML) and removed in be01992, which is why the
# bar read "HTML 80.8%" — Linguist had cached the tree from before the removal.
# Marked vendored so a future accidental commit cannot skew it again.
coverage/** linguist-vendored

# Raw k6 output. Committed on purpose as the evidence behind every latency claim,
# but it is machine-written and should be collapsed in diffs rather than reviewed
# line by line. SUMMARY.md and failure-attribution.txt are deliberately NOT
# listed here — those are the human-facing artifacts.
#
# The glob covers every phase directory rather than naming them one at a time, so
# a new phase's results are collapsed without anyone remembering to add a line.
# `.gitkeep.md` is re-included because it is written by hand.
benchmarks/*/results/** linguist-generated
benchmarks/*/results/.gitkeep.md -linguist-generated

# drizzle-kit writes these; they are not hand-authored SQL.
drizzle/** linguist-generated
